        -- Shows configuration for user pool email message MFA and sign-in with one-time
        -- passwords (OTPs). Includes the subject and body of the email message template for
        -- sign-in and MFA messages. To activate this setting, your user pool must be in the
        -- Essentials tier or higher.
        EmailMfaConfiguration: EmailMfaConfigType
        -- Displays the state of multi-factor authentication (MFA) as on, off, or optional. When
        -- ON, all users must set up MFA before they can sign in. When
        -- OPTIONAL, your application must make a client-side determination of
        -- whether a user wants to register an MFA device. For user pools with adaptive
